<i>♪ The future's
not ours to see ♪</i>

99
00:05:35,989 --> 00:05:40,429
<i>♪ Que Sera Sera ♪</i>

100
00:05:40,828 --> 00:05:43,788
<i>♪ What will
be will be ♪</i>

101
00:05:53,211 --> 00:05:57,912
<i>♪ Now I have
children of my own ♪</i>

102
00:05:58,019 --> 00:06:00,152
<i>♪ They ask
their father ♪</i>

103
00:06:00,282 --> 00:06:03,982
<i>♪ "What will I be?" ♪</i>

104
00:06:04,112 --> 00:06:06,463
<i>♪ "Will I be pretty?" ♪</i>

105
00:06:06,548 --> 00:06:08,855
<i>♪ "Will I
be rich?" ♪</i>

106
00:06:08,940 --> 00:06:12,727
<i>♪ I tell them
tenderly ♪</i>

107
00:06:12,868 --> 00:06:17,003
<i>♪ Que Sera Sera ♪</i>

108
00:06:17,212 --> 00:06:22,087
<i>♪ Whatever will be
wll be ♪</i>

109
00:06:22,217 --> 00:06:26,004
<i>♪ The future's not
ours to see ♪</i>

110
00:06:26,134 --> 00:06:31,096
<i>♪ Que Sera Sera ♪</i>

111
00:06:31,226 --> 00:06:36,144
<i>♪ What will be will be ♪</i>

112
00:06:36,275 --> 00:06:39,471
<i>♪ Que Sera Sera ♪</i>

113
00:06:39,556 --> 00:06:45,170
[Song continues
to play]

114
00:06:58,167 --> 00:06:59,995
[Clears throat]

115
00:07:22,333 --> 00:07:24,074
You hungry, Frank?

116
00:07:24,887 --> 00:07:26,367
Anything you need?

117
00:07:30,801 --> 00:07:32,565
Look.

118
00:07:32,740 --> 00:07:34,465
It's important for you
to understand that

119
00:07:34,550 --> 00:07:38,423
what happens tonight...
it's not personal.

120
00:07:40,427 --> 00:07:42,211
I know.

121
00:07:45,214 --> 00:07:47,695
[Frank] She liked you.

122
00:07:48,119 --> 00:07:50,219
Lauren.

123
00:07:50,738 --> 00:07:52,131
She always liked you.

124
00:07:53,801 --> 00:07:56,523
She said you were hard on people
'cause you had to be.

125
00:07:58,424 --> 00:08:01,122
That you made the decisions
other people couldn't.

126
00:08:04,016 --> 00:08:05,896
You're the one who was gonna
get everybody home.

127
00:08:11,812 --> 00:08:13,336
[Sighs]

128
00:08:15,414 --> 00:08:16,937
[Sighs]

129
00:08:19,761 --> 00:08:21,892
I wasn't always
like this, you know.

130
00:08:24,079 --> 00:08:26,003
None of us were.

131
00:08:27,994 --> 00:08:29,735
Look.

132
00:08:29,820 --> 00:08:31,784
If there's anything
you need,

133
00:08:32,148 --> 00:08:34,324
anyone
you wanna see, maybe,

134
00:08:35,264 --> 00:08:37,408
tie up loose ends...

135
00:08:38,933 --> 00:08:40,712
There is one thing
I'd like to do.

136
00:08:42,665 --> 00:08:45,249
So, you're telling me
that right now

137
00:08:45,579 --> 00:08:48,103
I'm in a town I can't leave,

138
00:08:48,234 --> 00:08:50,367
and that every night
when the sun goes down,

139
00:08:50,452 --> 00:08:53,886
monsters come from
the forest to hunt us?

140
00:08:54,828 --> 00:08:56,786
Monsters who, incidentally,

141
00:08:57,084 --> 00:08:58,668
killed my friend
the other night.

142
00:08:59,271 --> 00:09:00,372
Yeah.

143
00:09:04,953 --> 00:09:06,477
Yeah.

144
00:09:10,909 --> 00:09:12,301
Fuck off.

145
00:09:15,972 --> 00:09:17,040
[Laughs]

146
00:09:17,125 --> 00:09:20,333
This is... this is something.

147
00:09:20,527 --> 00:09:22,315
Where did he... where did he
find you?

148
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:23,617
Who?

149
00:09:23,748 --> 00:09:25,693
Tobey.
Are you guys individual hires,

150
00:09:25,778 --> 00:09:27,406
or is this one of
those traveling companies?

151
00:09:27,490 --> 00:09:29,797
'Cause, I mean, you play
the whole thing pretty great.

152
00:09:29,928 --> 00:09:31,275
I buy it.

153
00:09:32,293 --> 00:09:33,405
Not him so much. I just...

154
00:09:33,490 --> 00:09:35,146
I thought you were trying
a little bit too hard.

155
00:09:35,230 --> 00:09:36,449
But otherwise, I...

156
00:09:37,392 --> 00:09:38,893
[Laughs]

157
00:09:39,024 --> 00:09:41,330
Bravo.
Oh. Money well spent.

158
00:09:41,461 --> 00:09:43,380
So, uh, okay.

159
00:09:43,465 --> 00:09:45,641
So, what's next?
Is there, uh...

160
00:09:45,726 --> 00:09:47,902
Is there, like, some kind of
puzzle I have to solve?

161
00:09:48,357 --> 00:09:49,469
Mmm.

162
00:09:49,599 --> 00:09:51,343
Actually, you know what?
Never mind. Don't...

163
00:09:51,427 --> 00:09:54,117
- don't spoil it for me.
- Where are you going?

164
00:09:55,736 --> 00:09:57,132
Well, I'm not gonna
solve the puzzle

165
00:09:57,216 --> 00:09:58,434
sitting here all day.

166
00:09:58,565 --> 00:10:00,262
I'm gonna, you know,
check out the town,

167
00:10:00,377 --> 00:10:01,610
turn over a few stones.

168
00:10:01,695 --> 00:10:02,969
[Laughs]

169
00:10:03,054 --> 00:10:05,095
Fuck. Fuckin' Tobey.

170
00:10:05,180 --> 00:10:07,042
This must have cost a fortune.

171
00:10:09,358 --> 00:10:10,884
You want me to keep
an eye on him?

172
00:10:10,969 --> 00:10:12,622
No.

173
00:10:12,753 --> 00:10:14,482
Let him wander around town
for a while.

174
00:10:14,590 --> 00:10:16,244
We got enough
to deal with here.

175
00:10:16,329 --> 00:10:19,855
[Indistinct chatter]

176
00:10:20,195 --> 00:10:21,719
Ha.

177
00:10:25,113 --> 00:10:26,621
Okay.

178
00:10:26,894 --> 00:10:28,521
It's not quite
my Giacometti,

179
00:10:28,606 --> 00:10:31,085
but, uh, it'll do.

180
00:10:31,205 --> 00:10:32,816
Oh, perfect!

181
00:10:33,001 --> 00:10:35,003
Is that for me?

182
00:10:35,088 --> 00:10:36,611
Excuse me?

183
00:10:36,696 --> 00:10:39,786
Hey. Do you, uh... do you have
anything motorized,

184
00:10:40,188 --> 00:10:42,457
- like a scooter or something?
- What? No.

185
00:10:42,542 --> 00:10:43,924
- No? Okay. This'll do.
- I...

186
00:10:44,032 --> 00:10:46,618
- Thank you.
- No, that's my... Uh...

187
00:10:58,659 --> 00:11:01,340
Hey, buddy.

188
00:11:01,425 --> 00:11:03,371
Can I go outside today?

189
00:11:03,456 --> 00:11:04,977
Oh, honey.

190
00:11:05,077 --> 00:11:07,505
You need to stay in bed
a little longer.

191
00:11:07,590 --> 00:11:10,158
I'm tired
of staying in bed.

192
00:11:10,289 --> 00:11:13,382
And I don't like these pajamas.

193
00:11:13,480 --> 00:11:15,896
They're itchy
and they don't fit right.

194
00:11:15,981 --> 00:11:16,950
Oh, come on.

195
00:11:17,035 --> 00:11:18,764
Your dad went to the RV
to get our stuff.

196
00:11:18,849 --> 00:11:20,978
So tonight you're gonna sleep
in your own pajamas.

197
00:11:21,063 --> 00:11:22,500
We all should've gone.

198
00:11:22,997 --> 00:11:25,152
Well, we thought it was best
if Dad went on his own.

199
00:11:25,237 --> 00:11:26,787
Well, I don't like people
going through my stuff.

200
00:11:26,871 --> 00:11:28,089
Nobody's gonna do that.

201
00:11:28,220 --> 00:11:29,288
Yeah, okay.

202
00:11:29,373 --> 00:11:31,419
How long
are we gonna be here?

203
00:11:31,701 --> 00:11:34,922
We are, uh...
we're figuring that out.

204
00:11:36,402 --> 00:11:39,144
Hey. You hungry?

205
00:11:39,274 --> 00:11:40,670
I saw they're making eggs.
Do you want some eggs?

206
00:11:40,754 --> 00:11:43,235
Hobo eggs?

207
00:11:43,365 --> 00:11:44,497
No. No, no, no.
No hobo eggs.

208
00:11:44,627 --> 00:11:46,673
But they have oatmeal.

209
00:11:46,804 --> 00:11:48,718
Okay.

210
00:11:48,849 --> 00:11:50,764
What about you? You hungry?

211
00:11:50,895 --> 00:11:53,158
Uh, no. I think I'm just
gonna go for a walk.

212
00:11:53,288 --> 00:11:54,550
- Okay. Stay close.
- Yeah.

213
00:11:57,597 --> 00:12:00,643
I am going to get you
your oatmeal.

214
00:12:00,774 --> 00:12:02,341
Stay there.

215
00:12:15,354 --> 00:12:18,444
<i>Both speaking Cantonese...</i>

216
00:12:29,847 --> 00:12:31,152
[Plate smashes]

217
00:12:47,386 --> 00:12:48,953
Oh, jeez.

218
00:13:25,163 --> 00:13:26,555
You okay?

219
00:13:30,690 --> 00:13:32,910
Here.
Let me get that.

220
00:13:59,849 --> 00:14:00,981
One...

221
00:14:03,853 --> 00:14:05,246
three...

222
00:14:05,377 --> 00:14:08,075
four, five.

223
00:14:18,868 --> 00:14:20,174
Berries?

224
00:14:20,305 --> 00:14:21,610
I'm okay.

225
00:14:24,744 --> 00:14:27,268
There's an apple tree out back
if you'd prefer that.

226
00:14:29,662 --> 00:14:32,273
I see you grow
your own food.

227
00:14:32,404 --> 00:14:34,493
Supermarkets around here
are terrible, so...

228
00:14:38,976 --> 00:14:40,629
Oh.
[Chuckles]

229
00:14:40,760 --> 00:14:42,675
You're joking.

230
00:14:43,850 --> 00:14:45,504
Ellis and your dad
are gonna be back soon.

231
00:14:45,634 --> 00:14:46,940
You'll feel a lot better

232
00:14:47,071 --> 00:14:48,724
once you have
some of your own things.

233
00:14:48,855 --> 00:14:50,465
Yeah, I guess.

234
00:14:52,337 --> 00:14:53,381
Hey.

235
00:14:55,470 --> 00:14:57,037
You doing okay?

236
00:14:59,387 --> 00:15:02,390
No. Not really.

237
00:15:02,521 --> 00:15:04,218
Come here.

238
00:15:16,578 --> 00:15:17,623
All right.

239
00:15:17,753 --> 00:15:20,452
Let's see
what we got here, bud.

240
00:15:20,582 --> 00:15:22,845
I heard you were getting
a little itchy, so...

241
00:15:22,976 --> 00:15:24,760
Thank you, Dad.

242
00:15:24,891 --> 00:15:26,371
You're welcome.

243
00:15:27,894 --> 00:15:30,897
Um, how did it go?

244
00:15:31,028 --> 00:15:34,857
It was, uh...
it was good.

245
00:15:34,988 --> 00:15:36,555
Yeah?

246
00:15:36,685 --> 00:15:38,470
Are my books in there?

247
00:15:38,600 --> 00:15:40,695
Oh.

248
00:15:40,780 --> 00:15:43,649
Books!
How did I forget books?

249
00:15:43,779 --> 00:15:44,867
Dad...

250
00:15:44,998 --> 00:15:46,956
Oh, let's see.
Maybe there's one.

251
00:15:47,087 --> 00:15:48,697
Maybe I can find something.

252
00:15:48,828 --> 00:15:51,874
Oh, wait a minute.
We have books.

253
00:15:52,005 --> 00:15:54,834
What do we want?

254
00:15:54,964 --> 00:15:58,490
Do we want Adventures of
the Grand Gooligog?

255
00:16:00,492 --> 00:16:01,710
Flight of the Cromenockle?

256
00:16:01,841 --> 00:16:03,756
- [Gasps]
- [Tabitha] Ah. The Cromenockle.

257
00:16:03,886 --> 00:16:05,366
That's my favorite.

258
00:16:05,497 --> 00:16:07,107
Make the sound.

259
00:16:07,238 --> 00:16:11,546
Make the sound? I have no idea
what you're even... doo-ooh!

260
00:16:11,677 --> 00:16:13,374
[Giggles]

261
00:16:13,505 --> 00:16:14,810
[Giggles]

262
00:16:14,941 --> 00:16:17,639
[Makes otherworldly bird noise]

263
00:16:20,077 --> 00:16:21,817
[Laughs]

264
00:16:21,948 --> 00:16:24,516
[Makes otherworldly bird noise]

265
00:16:24,646 --> 00:16:27,345
She doesn't sound like that.

266
00:16:27,475 --> 00:16:29,825
No?
Does it sound like...

267
00:16:29,956 --> 00:16:31,740
[Makes otherworldly bird noise]

268
00:16:31,871 --> 00:16:34,961
No. Stop. Stop it.

269
00:16:35,092 --> 00:16:36,832
Okay, okay, okay.

270
00:16:36,963 --> 00:16:38,272
There's gonna be two
Cromenockles for you.

271
00:16:38,356 --> 00:16:39,705
Two.

272
00:16:39,835 --> 00:16:42,273
[They make
otherworldly bird noises]

273
00:16:42,403 --> 00:16:46,494
[Ethan laughs]

274
00:16:46,625 --> 00:16:48,366
Two Cromenockles for the cave.

275
00:16:48,496 --> 00:16:50,716
- Two Cromenockles for you.
- [Laughs]

276
00:16:50,846 --> 00:16:52,979
[Tabitha]
Careful with your leg.

277
00:16:53,110 --> 00:16:56,287
Julie, look.
We got our stuff.

278
00:16:56,417 --> 00:16:57,810
Yeah. So I see.

279
00:16:57,940 --> 00:17:00,682
- Hey, come here.
- Julie!

280
00:17:00,813 --> 00:17:02,554
We're reading the Cromenockle.

281
00:17:02,684 --> 00:17:03,772
Julie!

282
00:17:03,903 --> 00:17:06,166
[Makes otherworldly
bird noise]

283
00:17:06,434 --> 00:17:09,015
- Yeah. It's really funny.
- [Donna] Hey.

284
00:17:09,100 --> 00:17:10,754
Uh, sorry to interrupt.

285
00:17:10,910 --> 00:17:12,129
Father Khatri is here

286
00:17:12,259 --> 00:17:14,131
to talk to you about
the choosing ceremony.

287
00:17:14,695 --> 00:17:16,350
What's the
choosing ceremony?

288
00:17:16,481 --> 00:17:18,294
I'll let him fill you in.

289
00:17:18,379 --> 00:17:20,599
All newcomers have to decide
where they're gonna live.

290
00:17:20,684 --> 00:17:23,753
Here in Colony House
or down in the town.

291
00:17:23,838 --> 00:17:25,603
It's just part of
how we do things here.

292
00:17:25,688 --> 00:17:28,909
I'd like to take the both
of you, show you around.

293
00:17:29,123 --> 00:17:30,883
Maybe take you to the house
you'd be staying in,

294
00:17:30,967 --> 00:17:32,196
should you choose the town.

295
00:17:32,281 --> 00:17:34,413
Well, I wanna come.

296
00:17:34,934 --> 00:17:36,805
[Julie] What?
This is about all of us, right?

297
00:17:36,936 --> 00:17:37,752
I wanna see.

298
00:17:37,837 --> 00:17:39,408
We need you to stay here
and be with Ethan.

299
00:17:39,492 --> 00:17:41,799
Donna can watch Ethan.

300
00:17:44,465 --> 00:17:46,331
Okay. Fine.

301
00:17:47,135 --> 00:17:49,442
You guys go ahead.

302
00:17:50,325 --> 00:17:51,413
Hey.

303
00:17:52,289 --> 00:17:53,822
We won't be gone long.

304
00:17:53,953 --> 00:17:55,346
Okay.

305
00:17:56,558 --> 00:17:57,615
[Tabitha]
You know what?

306
00:17:57,700 --> 00:17:59,789
Maybe I should stay.
I shouldn't leave her alone.

307
00:17:59,874 --> 00:18:02,912
I think it's very important
that both of you see this.

308
00:18:02,997 --> 00:18:04,564
It's gonna be okay.

309
00:18:04,703 --> 00:18:06,076
She's a tough kid.

310
00:18:06,161 --> 00:18:07,336
Takes after her mother.

311
00:18:07,836 --> 00:18:10,380
- [Scoffs]
- Come.

312
00:18:14,016 --> 00:18:15,757
[Tires grind on gravel]

313
00:18:20,675 --> 00:18:24,984
[Indistinct chatter]

314
00:18:25,114 --> 00:18:27,726
[Laughs]

315
00:18:27,856 --> 00:18:29,461
Good morning, everybody.

316
00:18:29,546 --> 00:18:32,201
What's cooking today, huh?

317
00:18:32,286 --> 00:18:33,809
[Laughs]

318
00:18:34,298 --> 00:18:35,734
Is this where I find
my next clue?

319
00:18:35,864 --> 00:18:37,214
Is this where the, uh...

320
00:18:37,344 --> 00:18:39,486
Is this where the monsters
jump from the shadows?

321
00:18:39,571 --> 00:18:43,515
Uh, "Oh, what wonders
will avail themselves

322
00:18:43,600 --> 00:18:47,184
in the quaint little
roadside diner

323
00:18:47,269 --> 00:18:50,707
in which my guard
hath fallen?"

324
00:18:50,792 --> 00:18:51,960
Huh?

325
00:18:52,045 --> 00:18:54,027
I did some summer stock
back in the day.

326
00:18:54,112 --> 00:18:56,581
Not bad, right?
Oh, thank you. I'm starving.

327
00:18:56,666 --> 00:18:58,886
- What've we got?
- Hey. There's a line.

328
00:18:58,974 --> 00:19:00,613
Look. I'm all
for authenticity,

329
00:19:00,705 --> 00:19:01,691
but I'm also
really hungry,

330
00:19:01,776 --> 00:19:03,216
and since y'all basically
work for me anyways,

331
00:19:03,300 --> 00:19:04,726
it's kind of okay.

332
00:19:04,896 --> 00:19:06,027
Ow. What the...

333
00:19:06,112 --> 00:19:08,708
<i>Speaks Cantonese...</i>

334
00:19:08,793 --> 00:19:10,150
[Laughs]

335
00:19:10,285 --> 00:19:11,486
<i>Speaks Cantonese...</i>

336
00:19:11,571 --> 00:19:13,051
All right. Jeez.

337
00:19:13,136 --> 00:19:15,051
People really
take all this seriously.

338
00:19:23,912 --> 00:19:26,959
What are you doing here?

339
00:19:27,089 --> 00:19:29,266
You promised
you'd stay home.

340
00:19:29,396 --> 00:19:31,616
If I didn't show up,
they would have wondered why.

341
00:19:31,746 --> 00:19:33,835
It'll be okay. I wanna help.

342
00:19:33,966 --> 00:19:36,751
- Sara...
- I need to help.

343
00:19:38,840 --> 00:19:41,190
You should get back to the barn.

344
00:19:41,321 --> 00:19:43,715
- It'll be okay.
- Sara...

345
00:19:43,845 --> 00:19:46,674
I promise.

346
00:19:55,466 --> 00:19:58,295
[Khatri] It's the talismans
that keep them out.

347
00:19:58,425 --> 00:20:00,775
Now, there are a number of
other precautions people take.

348
00:20:00,906 --> 00:20:02,777
Nailing the windows shut,
for instance.

349
00:20:02,908 --> 00:20:04,823
With a child in the house,
this is a must.

350
00:20:04,953 --> 00:20:06,433
Why?

351
00:20:06,564 --> 00:20:09,044
Well, there'll be nights
where these... these things,

352
00:20:09,175 --> 00:20:12,918
they'll try to convince you
to let them in.

353
00:20:13,048 --> 00:20:16,051
And children tend to be
most susceptible.

354
00:20:16,182 --> 00:20:20,229
How are people walking around
like all this is normal?

355
00:20:20,360 --> 00:20:21,970
Well, the people
who survive here

356
00:20:22,101 --> 00:20:24,321
are the ones who adapt.

357
00:20:24,451 --> 00:20:26,845
How exactly
do they do that?

358
00:20:26,975 --> 00:20:30,544
The way someone who lives
on a fault line, for example.

359
00:20:30,675 --> 00:20:31,719
They adapt to the notion

360
00:20:31,850 --> 00:20:32,764
that the earth
could just open up

361
00:20:32,894 --> 00:20:35,070
and swallow them
at any given moment.

362
00:20:35,201 --> 00:20:36,855
They go on with their lives

363
00:20:36,985 --> 00:20:40,424
because that reality is a part
of the world that they live in.

364
00:20:40,578 --> 00:20:43,015
Look. I wish there was
an explanation I could give you

365
00:20:43,114 --> 00:20:44,724
that would make
any of this easier.

366
00:20:44,863 --> 00:20:46,908
But it's gonna be fine.

367
00:20:47,039 --> 00:20:49,694
Okay? Just always remember.

368
00:20:49,824 --> 00:20:52,174
Place the talisman by the door.
Cover your windows.

369
00:20:52,305 --> 00:20:54,351
Nail your windows shut.

370
00:20:54,481 --> 00:20:57,745
You do these things, your
family's going to be just fine.

371
00:20:57,876 --> 00:20:59,965
Hey. Um, I'm sorry.
What's that?

372
00:21:05,797 --> 00:21:08,669
Um, we call that the box.

373
00:21:08,800 --> 00:21:12,456
It's our only form
of punishment we have here.

374
00:21:12,586 --> 00:21:16,982
You see, the rules we live by
are meant to protect each other,

375
00:21:17,112 --> 00:21:18,940
to keep each other safe.

376
00:21:19,071 --> 00:21:21,856
And when someone's
actions or negligence

377
00:21:21,987 --> 00:21:24,772
leads to the death
of a resident in town,

378
00:21:24,903 --> 00:21:28,950
the only punishment for that
crime is a night in the box.

379
00:21:31,126 --> 00:21:32,606
Jesus.

380
00:21:32,737 --> 00:21:35,130
But you keep one of those
talismans in there, right?

381
00:21:35,261 --> 00:21:36,567
No.

382
00:21:39,134 --> 00:21:40,745
How many times
have you used it?

383
00:21:42,921 --> 00:21:44,923
Tonight will be the first.

384
00:21:46,968 --> 00:21:48,970
Look. Come.

385
00:21:49,101 --> 00:21:51,277
- Your house is just up ahead.
- Yeah.

386
00:21:51,408 --> 00:21:53,192
[Door hinge squeaks]

387
00:21:56,155 --> 00:21:59,057
So, it's not much,
but it'll keep you comfortable

388
00:21:59,142 --> 00:22:00,839
if you choose to live in town.

389
00:22:05,312 --> 00:22:08,343
Looks like somebody's
already living here.

390
00:22:11,995 --> 00:22:15,390
Um, there was a...

391
00:22:15,521 --> 00:22:20,572
There was an incident
the night before you arrived.

392
00:22:22,038 --> 00:22:23,909
The first we'd had in months.

393
00:22:25,398 --> 00:22:27,269
What kind of incident?

394
00:22:27,701 --> 00:22:30,225
The kind that happens
when people are careless.

395
00:22:50,989 --> 00:22:53,600
It was a child?

396
00:22:53,731 --> 00:22:55,297
Holy fuck.

397
00:22:55,428 --> 00:22:57,604
Meagan and her mother Lauren.

398
00:22:59,998 --> 00:23:02,740
The father was
passed out drunk

399
00:23:02,870 --> 00:23:04,524
at the other end of town
when it happened.

400
00:23:06,483 --> 00:23:10,225
This is what happens
when you break the rules.

401
00:23:21,062 --> 00:23:22,194
Tabitha, wait.

402
00:23:22,324 --> 00:23:23,404
No, Jim, I'm sorry.
I can't.

403
00:23:23,500 --> 00:23:25,153
I can't do that right now.

404
00:23:25,284 --> 00:23:26,804
You make it seem like
we have a choice.

405
00:23:26,894 --> 00:23:28,287
Jim.

406
00:23:28,417 --> 00:23:30,507
Jim, this is
fucking insane!

407
00:23:30,637 --> 00:23:33,422
That woman and her little girl
were ripped apart.

408
00:23:33,553 --> 00:23:35,860
Now they're putting the dad
in some fucking box at sundown

409
00:23:35,990 --> 00:23:36,990
for those things to...

410
00:23:37,078 --> 00:23:39,864
You heard
what the priest said.

411
00:23:39,994 --> 00:23:41,216
If he'd have followed
the rules,

412
00:23:41,300 --> 00:23:44,259
they'd all still be alive
right now.

413
00:23:44,390 --> 00:23:46,958
Jim? Why are you...
Why are you so eager

414
00:23:47,088 --> 00:23:49,264
to take any of this
at face value, Jim?

415
00:23:52,694 --> 00:23:54,838
Because I can still hear
those things whispering

416
00:23:54,922 --> 00:23:56,184
outside the RV.

417
00:23:56,315 --> 00:23:59,361
I can still hear them
tapping on the glass.

418
00:23:59,492 --> 00:24:03,452
Tabby, whatever this is,
it's real, and we are stuck.

419
00:24:03,583 --> 00:24:05,846
So we better figure out a way
to make the best of it.

420
00:24:07,674 --> 00:24:10,068
'Cause we don't want to
end up like...

421
00:24:12,331 --> 00:24:14,072
No, no, no. No.

422
00:24:17,858 --> 00:24:19,947
[Birds chirp]

423
00:24:20,078 --> 00:24:21,993
[Twig snaps]

424
00:24:22,123 --> 00:24:24,038
This was Meagan's
favorite spot.

425
00:24:30,436 --> 00:24:32,003
Put this swing here for her,

426
00:24:32,133 --> 00:24:35,006
and she was
always wanting me

427
00:24:35,136 --> 00:24:37,799
to push her higher and higher,

428
00:24:37,891 --> 00:24:41,106
but... Lauren was afraid
it wasn't safe.

429
00:24:47,496 --> 00:24:50,369
You'll bury me next to them,
right?

430
00:24:50,499 --> 00:24:52,023
Yeah.

431
00:24:53,851 --> 00:24:54,982
Of course.

432
00:24:58,159 --> 00:25:00,161
Okay.

433
00:25:00,292 --> 00:25:01,946
I'll just be a few minutes here.

434
00:25:02,076 --> 00:25:04,078
Okay.
Take whatever time you need.

435
00:25:28,407 --> 00:25:30,322
All right, little guy.

436
00:25:30,452 --> 00:25:32,212
Give that a try
and let me know how it feels.

437
00:25:37,895 --> 00:25:39,157
Feel good?

438
00:25:39,287 --> 00:25:41,420
It hurts my armpit.

439
00:25:41,550 --> 00:25:43,640
Oh, it hurts your armpit?
Okay. Hold on.

440
00:25:43,770 --> 00:25:47,426
Here. I'll add a little
extra padding there for you,

441
00:25:47,556 --> 00:25:50,124
and if this feels good,
I'll tie it on later, okay?

442
00:25:50,255 --> 00:25:51,299
Here. Try that.

443
00:25:53,084 --> 00:25:54,520
Ready? Here.

444
00:25:54,651 --> 00:25:56,217
Let's go
down the stairs here.

445
00:25:56,348 --> 00:25:57,871
Take your time.
There you go, buddy.

446
00:25:58,002 --> 00:26:00,787
Come on. Three, two, one.

447
00:26:02,049 --> 00:26:03,049
Boom!

448
00:26:04,138 --> 00:26:05,226
He's adorable.

449
00:26:06,750 --> 00:26:08,490
Why are you doing this?

450
00:26:08,621 --> 00:26:10,014
What do you mean?

451
00:26:10,144 --> 00:26:11,798
You guys barely know us.

452
00:26:14,758 --> 00:26:16,237
It's just what we do.

453
00:26:23,592 --> 00:26:25,769
It's, like,
the ultimate escape room.

454
00:26:25,899 --> 00:26:28,419
I mean, seriously, I don't know
how he pulled all this together.

455
00:26:28,510 --> 00:26:31,035
So, um, I'm thinking

456
00:26:31,165 --> 00:26:33,951
maybe there's a clue
in each one of the buildings?

457
00:26:34,081 --> 00:26:36,127
Hmm?
Am I getting warmer?

458
00:26:36,257 --> 00:26:38,210
'Cause I mean, usually,
you know,

459
00:26:38,295 --> 00:26:40,395
you have some type of prompt
that lets you know

460
00:26:40,479 --> 00:26:42,350
which direction to go.
But this is, uh...

461
00:26:42,481 --> 00:26:44,265
This is just
some next-level shit.

462
00:26:46,224 --> 00:26:48,139
Has, uh...

463
00:26:48,269 --> 00:26:52,360
Has anyone
talked to you yet?

464
00:26:52,491 --> 00:26:56,234
Yeah. The lady up at the, uh,
big house. Donna.

465
00:26:56,364 --> 00:26:58,105
I mean, she gave me
the whole intro.

466
00:26:58,236 --> 00:26:59,803
You know,
the monsters in the forest.

467
00:26:59,933 --> 00:27:02,762
Tobey's dead. Blah, blah, blah.
But she didn't give me any hints

468
00:27:02,893 --> 00:27:04,375
about where I'm supposed to go
next. Here's the thing, though.

469
00:27:04,459 --> 00:27:06,984
Like, as thorough
as all this feels,

470
00:27:07,114 --> 00:27:09,334
there's a couple flaws
in the logic.

471
00:27:09,464 --> 00:27:11,989
I'm sitting here eating eggs
in a diner

472
00:27:12,119 --> 00:27:14,165
in a place that's
supposed to be, what,

473
00:27:14,295 --> 00:27:15,993
some kind of
mystical nightmare?

474
00:27:16,123 --> 00:27:17,603
I mean,
I don't know about you,

475
00:27:17,734 --> 00:27:20,006
but my nightmares
don't usually serve breakfast.

476
00:27:20,091 --> 00:27:21,346
I suppose you're gonna tell me
you've got chickens

477
00:27:21,430 --> 00:27:22,953
roaming around
in the big bad forest?

478
00:27:23,038 --> 00:27:24,965
Yeah, but the chickens,
the cows?

479
00:27:25,050 --> 00:27:27,096
We don't really know
where they come from.

480
00:27:27,656 --> 00:27:29,136
Mmm.

481
00:27:30,841 --> 00:27:32,801
That's actually not bad
for a nightmare breakfast.

482
00:27:35,517 --> 00:27:37,780
I should probably get going.

483
00:27:41,492 --> 00:27:43,802
Am I supposed to get anything
from you?

484
00:27:44,586 --> 00:27:46,327
What?

485
00:27:46,458 --> 00:27:48,923
I don't know. Like a clue

486
00:27:49,008 --> 00:27:53,378
or some kind of
cryptic direction?

487
00:27:53,508 --> 00:27:57,167
You know what? Never mind.
I'll figure it out.

488
00:27:59,373 --> 00:28:02,158
Thanks.

489
00:28:09,568 --> 00:28:12,484
- Was that...
- The guy from the other car.

490
00:28:12,614 --> 00:28:14,957
He's gonna get himself killed.

491
00:28:15,100 --> 00:28:18,222
Um, are you hungry?
Have you eaten anything yet?

492
00:28:18,307 --> 00:28:20,553
No, I'm fine. I just came
to check on you guys.

493
00:28:20,638 --> 00:28:21,639
Right.

494
00:28:22,799 --> 00:28:24,235
[Speaks Cantonese]

495
00:28:26,063 --> 00:28:28,152
Okay.

496
00:28:28,282 --> 00:28:30,241
How's she doing?

497
00:28:30,331 --> 00:28:32,445
Well, she's...

498
00:28:32,570 --> 00:28:35,289
Uh, like I said, denial is a
major part of our family tree.

499
00:28:45,560 --> 00:28:47,432
Let's see, now.

500
00:28:47,562 --> 00:28:48,607
Twelve.

501
00:28:48,737 --> 00:28:51,305
Ten, 12.

502
00:28:52,480 --> 00:28:53,525
Okay.

503
00:28:55,222 --> 00:28:56,571
- [Paper crinkles]
- [Bird chirps]

504
00:29:07,626 --> 00:29:09,933
What are you doing?

505
00:29:11,238 --> 00:29:13,284
I don't think you're supposed
to be out here.

506
00:29:13,414 --> 00:29:14,633
Are you looking
for something?

507
00:29:14,763 --> 00:29:16,156
Go away.

508
00:29:16,287 --> 00:29:20,030
I can help you look.
I'm good at finding stuff.

509
00:29:20,160 --> 00:29:22,467
I'm not looking.

510
00:29:22,597 --> 00:29:24,643
I'm checking.

511
00:29:24,773 --> 00:29:26,863
What are you checking?

512
00:29:30,431 --> 00:29:32,129
You ask a lot of questions.

513
00:29:33,957 --> 00:29:35,567
That was only three.

514
00:29:37,351 --> 00:29:38,744
[Sighs]

515
